   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 234075,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 37421,
    "poster_id": 1991,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6ba3913be8bac15d6c3b89a5fc02f73181ce0261.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"11\" > <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/f/b4fef0a6ea1670d0b47c20aa14ee5b16b42cf183.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq i \\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" > be real numbers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22cb41daedb1d34585cdc23279d2899039b1c2d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" > Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"8\" height=\"11\" > be their symmetric sum of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\"  width=\"8\" height=\"12\" > respectively. Prove that:<br>\n<br>\ni) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/4/6e4390a0bfc5c4d781501350ce51747e819949e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 \\cdot \\frac{n-1}{n}-2q \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"37\" ><br>\n<br>\nii) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83c1cb44fee0def67e20376f8fb4ceba1fbd2558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|x_i - \\frac{p}{n}\\right| \\leq \\sqrt{p^2 - \\frac{2nq}{n-1}} \\cdot \\frac{n-1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"249\" height=\"43\" > for every meaningful <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\"  width=\"5\" height=\"12\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "Let $x_i,$ $1 \\leq i \\leq n$ be real numbers with $n \\geq 3.$ Let $p$ and $q$ be their symmetric sum of degree $1$ and $2$ respectively. Prove that:\r\n\r\ni) $p^2 \\cdot \\frac{n-1}{n}-2q \\geq 0$\r\n\r\nii) $\\left|x_i - \\frac{p}{n}\\right| \\leq \\sqrt{p^2 - \\frac{2nq}{n-1}} \\cdot \\frac{n-1}{n}$ for every meaningful $i$.",
